# Never send these to the build context. node_modules in particular is tens of
# thousands of files that the python stage's `COPY ./ .` would otherwise pull
# in, for no reason - the web stage installs its own from the lockfile.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.git/
# `.venv/` alone missed a sibling `.venv312/`, which `COPY ./ .` then baked in
# as a 43 MB layer - and because a later `rm -rf` cannot reclaim space from an
# earlier layer, it stayed in the image. CI builds from a clean checkout so
# published images were never affected, but anyone building locally shipped
# their own virtualenv. Glob the suffixed variants too.
.venv*/
venv*/
env/
certs/
config/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
